From: moWerk <mo@mowerk.net>
Subject: [PATCH] qmimodem: voicecall: register for call notifications

The QMI voice driver only listens for ALL CALL STATUS indications and
relies on the modem sending them to every client. The F(x)tec Pro1-X
modem (MPSS.HA.1.1 with its carrier MCFG) sends them only to clients
that registered for call notification events: a raw QMI client that
registered (VOICE INDICATION REGISTER, TLV 0x13) saw an incoming call go
through SETUP, INCOMING and END, an unregistered one and ofono saw
nothing, so the phone never rang. Register at probe, as ModemManager
does.

Tested on the Pro1-X (SailfishOS 5.2, mainline 7.3): incoming calls ring
and can be answered, with the screen on and from suspend.

---
diff --git a/drivers/qmimodem/voice.h b/drivers/qmimodem/voice.h
index 2c078137..835b99b9 100644
--- a/drivers/qmimodem/voice.h
+++ b/drivers/qmimodem/voice.h
@@ -39,6 +39,7 @@ enum qmi_ussd_user_required {
 /* QMI service voice. Using an enum to prevent doublicated entries */
 enum voice_commands {
 	QMI_VOICE_DIAL_CALL =			0x20,
+	QMI_VOICE_INDICATION_REGISTER =		0x03,
 	QMI_VOICE_ALL_CALL_STATUS_IND =		0x2e,
 	QMI_VOICE_GET_ALL_CALL_INFO =		0x2f,
 	QMI_VOICE_END_CALL =			0x21,
diff --git a/drivers/qmimodem/voicecall.c b/drivers/qmimodem/voicecall.c
index fe27502c..aa4ce46b 100644
--- a/drivers/qmimodem/voicecall.c
+++ b/drivers/qmimodem/voicecall.c
@@ -726,6 +726,7 @@ static int qmi_voicecall_probe(struct ofono_voicecall *vc,
 {
 	struct qmi_service *voice = user_data;
 	struct voicecall_data *data;
+	struct qmi_param *param;
 
 	DBG("");
 
@@ -736,6 +737,19 @@ static int qmi_voicecall_probe(struct ofono_voicecall *vc,
 	qmi_service_register(data->voice, QMI_VOICE_ALL_CALL_STATUS_IND,
 				all_call_status_ind, vc, NULL);
 
+	/*
+	 * Ask for call notifications explicitly (INDICATION REGISTER, TLV 0x13
+	 * "call notification events"). Some modems send ALL CALL STATUS only to
+	 * clients that registered for them: on the F(x)tec Pro1-X (MPSS.HA.1.1 with
+	 * its carrier MCFG) an incoming call reached a registered QMI client but
+	 * never ofono, so the phone did not ring. ModemManager registers the same way.
+	 */
+	param = qmi_param_new();
+	qmi_param_append_uint8(param, 0x13, 1);
+	if (!qmi_service_send(data->voice, QMI_VOICE_INDICATION_REGISTER, param,
+				NULL, NULL, NULL))
+		qmi_param_free(param);
+
 	ofono_voicecall_set_data(vc, data);
 
 	//Get a handle to the modem serial interface to detect RING signals
